## Layouts

Single-domain wiki:

```text
wiki/
├── SCHEMA.md
├── index.md
├── log.md
├── raw/
│   ├── sources/
│   ├── articles/
│   ├── papers/
│   ├── transcripts/
│   └── assets/
├── source-cards/
├── entities/
├── concepts/
├── comparisons/
└── queries/
```

Multi-domain wiki:

```text
wiki/
├── SCHEMA.md
├── index.md
├── log.md
├── _meta/
│   └── domains.md
└── domains/
    └── <domain>/
        ├── SCHEMA.md
        ├── index.md
        ├── log.md
        ├── raw/
        │   ├── sources/
        │   └── assets/
        ├── source-cards/
        ├── entities/
        ├── concepts/
        ├── comparisons/
        └── queries/
```

Use multi-domain structure when a topic has a different source universe, taxonomy, evaluation framework, or likely 10+ pages.

## Schema Template

````markdown
# Wiki Schema

## Domain
<what this wiki covers>

## Conventions
- File names use lowercase hyphen-case.
- Every wiki page starts with YAML frontmatter.
- Use [[wikilinks]] between pages.
- Update `updated` when materially changing a page.
- Add every active page to `index.md`.
- Append every material action to `log.md`.

## Frontmatter
```yaml
---
title: Page Title
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
type: entity | concept | comparison | query | summary
tags: [schema-owned-tags]
sources: [raw/sources/source-name.md]
---
```

## Tag Taxonomy
<define 10-20 domain tags before using them>

## Page Thresholds
- Create a page when an entity or concept appears in 2+ sources or is central to one source.
- Add to an existing page when a source mentions something already covered.
- Do not create pages for passing mentions.
- Split pages that become hard to scan.
- Archive fully superseded pages.
````

## Index Template

```markdown
# Wiki Index

> Content catalog. Every wiki page listed under its type with a one-line summary.
> Last updated: YYYY-MM-DD | Total pages: N

## Entities

## Concepts

## Comparisons

## Queries
```

When any section exceeds 50 entries, split it into sub-sections. When the whole index exceeds 200 entries, create a topic map.

## Log Template

```markdown
# Wiki Log

> Chronological record of wiki actions.
> Format: `## [YYYY-MM-DD] action | subject`
> Actions: ingest, update, query, lint, create, archive, delete, migrate

## [YYYY-MM-DD] create | Wiki initialized
- Domain: <domain>
- Structure created with SCHEMA.md, index.md, log.md
```

Rotate `log.md` when it exceeds 500 entries.

## Ingest Detail

1. Capture raw source first:
   - URL, article, X post, Gist, repo note, or structured API output: save markdown or JSON under `raw/sources/`.
   - PDF or paper: save under `raw/papers/`.
   - pasted text: save under the closest raw subfolder.
   - images/assets: save under `raw/assets/<source-slug>/`.
   - if full raw capture is inappropriate, save limited excerpts or retrieval metadata and explain the skip reason in the source card.
2. Create a compact source card under `source-cards/` when the source is worth preserving. It should point to the raw snapshot, canonical URL, retrieval method, neutral claim inventory, cautions, and related compiled pages.
3. Search existing pages and indexes for mentioned entities, concepts, and questions.
4. Create or update compiled pages that meet the schema threshold. Do not grow source cards into long article summaries.
5. Preserve contradiction instead of overwriting it: note both claims with dates and sources, and flag for review.
6. Keep synthesis preference-neutral unless the user explicitly stated a preference. Do not infer that the user wants or rejects a tactic because it is controversial, hypey, aggressive, or high-risk. Split the source into observed mechanics, risk gates, usable-with-constraints cases, and decisions requiring user review.
7. Use `do_not_apply` or "rejected" language only for non-negotiable blockers such as illegality, rights violations, privacy violations, unavoidable deception, or obvious platform/account evasion. Otherwise prefer constrained-candidate language.
8. Add useful outbound wikilinks from new pages when possible.
9. Update `index.md` once after the page set is stable.
10. Append a `log.md` entry listing files changed.

For bulk ingest, read all sources first, identify all entities/concepts in one pass, then update pages and index once.

## Query Detail

1. Read `index.md` to identify candidate pages.
2. Search all `.md` files when the wiki is large or terms may not appear in the index.
3. Read relevant compiled pages first, then raw snapshots or original sources when exact claims, evidence, wording, or currentness matter.
4. Synthesize the answer from compiled knowledge and verified source evidence.
5. Cite wiki pages using `[[wikilinks]]`.
6. File only reusable synthesis into `queries/`, `comparisons/`, or another compiled page. Source cards remain provenance/index records.
7. Append a query log entry.

## Lint Detail

Report findings by severity:
- broken wikilinks
- orphan pages
- pages missing from `index.md`
- invalid or incomplete frontmatter
- tags not present in `SCHEMA.md`
- contradictory claims needing review
- stale pages
- oversized pages
- log rotation needed

Use scripts or shell searches for large wikis instead of hand-inspecting every file.

## Archiving

1. Create `_archive/` if needed.
2. Move the superseded page while preserving a recognizable path.
3. Remove it from `index.md`.
4. Update inbound links to point at the replacement or plain archived note.
5. Log the archive.

## Obsidian Notes

The wiki should work as an Obsidian vault:
- `[[wikilinks]]` render as links.
- `raw/assets/` can store attachments.
- YAML frontmatter supports Dataview-style workflows when the user uses Obsidian.
